WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.134
It's the first of the month.

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.469
You know what that means:

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.470
Rent's due.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.144
What's up, guys?

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.479
I'm Tyrann Mathieu, also

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.580
known as The Landlord.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:14.781
They call me The Landlord

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.583
cuz I own the field and I take care of

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.785
Chiefs Kingdom. But right now my social

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.587
responsibility goes much beyond that.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:21.888
A lot of people have been

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.491
impacted by COVID-19, especially

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.859
in my hometown of New Orleans.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.761
I'm hoping to find a few families

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.029
that I can really impact and

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.597
help and love and support.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.065
I'm looking forward to checking them out.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.074
- I know you love New Orleans, and

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.242
I wanted to share with you a

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.443
family that could use your help.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.345
Courtney is an extremely talented

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.180
artist and a mother of twins with

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.617
autism. Her children are Lyric and Julius.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.986
Courtney is now a survivor of COVID-19.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.555
Courtney was diagnosed a few weeks back,

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.357
and I honestly remember her telling me

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.359
the hardest part of fighting the virus

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.261
was not being able to touch her children.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.896
She just hugged her son Julius

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.564
for the first time about a

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.200
week ago. And he was excited

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.003
and so was she. Thank you again, Tyrann.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.072
This would mean the world

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.840
to Lyric and their family.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.645
- Hey, how you doing?

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.647
- Hey, how you doing?

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.681
- It’s good to see you.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.216
- Good to see you too. My son is over here.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.452
- Is that Lyric?
- Yup, that's Lyric.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.457
- How's everybody doing? It's so

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.858
good to see you guys smiling.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.927
- We live in New Orleans.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:35.028
- Yeah.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.229
He's from New Orleans.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.497
- Yeah, I'm from New Orleans.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.232
So, I mean, how has everything been?

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.667
Um, cuz I, I mean, I've heard that

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:44.471
you tested positive for coronavirus now.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.572
How did that go for you?

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.773
Were you able to work?

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.408
- Well, I actually haven't been able to work

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:52.345
since before I was tested positive

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.781
because of them being home from school.
- Gotcha.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.685
- And then, um, my cousin got

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.320
sick, and she also lives with us.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.989
Unfortunately, she was hospitalized, but

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:06.426
I wasn't. I probably may have needed to

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.862
be, but I couldn't leave my kids at home.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.432
So we both fully recovered.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.534
Um, we still have the aftereffects.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.904
Sometimes I feel like I need, like,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.639
a breathing treatment from an asthma

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:22.909
pump, but that was in, like, March.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.611
I didn't get to hug them

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.813
until late April, early

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:27.180
May.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.517
So, can you imagine living in the same

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.252
house with your kids and not having

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.720
any kind of physical contact?

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.990
- I want to ask Lyric a question if she's listening.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:38.191
- Sure.
- Hi.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.360
- How was it, how was it for you

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.828
when, when your mom was sick

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.263
and she wasn't able to hug you?

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.532
How did that go for you?

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.734
- Since I wasn't able to hug my mom,

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.002
I hugged my brother a lot.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.537
- That's so good.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:51.905
I want to get personal

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:52.839
with you for a second.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.108
I want to ask you, cuz I, I

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.276
mean, I've heard, I've heard it.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.778
You've told me. You

00:02:58.778 --> 00:02:59.913
haven't been able to work.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.648
Um, you know, you've

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.849
been self-quarantined.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.418
How has it been financially for you?

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.487
- I was without a car for 10 years,

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.656
and on March 13, the day

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.591
before everything started

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:14.327
shutting down and everything, I bought a car.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.662
So now I have a car note.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.031
I have this

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.132
car insurance that's

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.333
higher than my car note.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:24.037
I'm behind on the water bill,

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.772
behind on the light bill.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.941
Um, and just trying to keep food in

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.510
the house. Man, these two teenagers

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.880
can eat you out of house and home.
- [Lyric laughing]

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.782
- Well, you, you know my nickname is

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.217
The Landlord, and I'm, and I'm

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.618
the person that runs the field.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.086
So I control everything.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.155
And then also I take care of the kingdom.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.056
So I'm always thinking

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.224
about my community and,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:48.161
and people in need. Um, and I've heard your story.

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:49.729
You just shared it with me.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.531
And I'm so grateful that

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:52.599
I was able to talk to you.

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:54.534
And I feel like you deserve so much

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.469
more—um, really everything you've,

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.171
you've been able to overcome.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.807
Um, I want to be able to help you.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:01.908
I want to show you some love.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.176
So right now I want you

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.110
to check your texts

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.545
for me, please, if you could.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:09.482
- Oh wow! Thank you!

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.584
- You're welcome.
- Thank you so, so much.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.354
- So, I sent you one month's rent, and

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.089
then my friends at Zelle, they were

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.558
able to donate the next month's rent.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.492
So you're actually going to be

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.294
covered for the next two months.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.929
You know, I love my community.

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.464
And so any time I'm able to hear

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.833
stories like this, I always want to

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.201
be a part of those people's lives.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.270
Cuz it always helps change mine.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.839
Um, so it was good talking to you today.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.040
It was good seeing you guys.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.042
And I wish you guys

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.043
the best going forward.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.845
I wish you guys much, much health.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:39.779
- And to you.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.382
- And thank you. Thank you so much for looking out.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.117
You know, not everybody's out there

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:47.420
looking out for the little people, you know.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.155
Thank you so much for looking out for me.
- Thank you.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.491
- And, and these two little ones I

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:54.727
got right here. They're 15, but they're still little ones.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.996
- Yes, yes. They'll always be your babies.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.098
- Yes. Always. Always.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:05.905
- Bye.
- Bye-bye. Take care.

